    "body": "Experimental test update with optional estimated sleep, off by default. Requires Android 10+ and compatible Google Play services for sleep estimates; the alarm app still supports Android 8+. Phone light and movement are estimates, not proof of sleep. No REM/stage/medical claim. No microphone, camera or location permission. No automatic alarm-time changes.\n\nSleep records stay in private app storage and can be cleared. Copy summary is an explicit clipboard action. Enabling estimates adds a Google Play services provider dependency; provider delivery and physical-device overnight accuracy remain unverified.\n\nCorrects locked-boot alarm recovery while preserving existing credential-private pairing, keys, alarms and sound preferences. An alarm-only device-protected mirror and private copy of the exact selected sound support ringing before unlock. If the selected sound cannot be cached, that limitation is reported rather than silently substituting another tone.\n\nThe exact APK below passed synthetic API34 in-place upgrades from the actual signed0.1.4 in both chosen-sound and unchanged-default modes, secure cold reboot and pre-unlock looping alarm playback, dismissal/unlock reconciliation and old-code rollback compatibility. Rollback testing used old code with a higher test-only version code because Android blocks direct downgrade; that fixture is not released. Ordinary unit and alarm-flow emulator checks also passed. This does not establish physical-phone reliability. Keep an independent backup alarm.\n\nInstall over the existing app without uninstalling or clearing data. Open once after updating. Sleep estimates remain optional and off until explicitly enabled.\n\nSHA-256: 8550ba9651f5ee2bbd5ed08c893d8121a4331f33bf196648b1c879d631a60ce5"
